  "question": {
    "text": "Three balls of masses $2 \\mathrm{~kg}, 4 \\mathrm{~kg}$ and $6 \\mathrm{~kg}$ respectively are arranged at centre of the edges of an equilateral triangle of side $2 \\mathrm{~m}$. The moment of intertia of the system about an axis through the centroid and perpendicular to the plane of triangle, will be _______ $\\mathrm{kg} \\mathrm{m}^2$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/Y9HoriFGYNLWkpL6wZWw1CIGBPr66In48QGPDPzd9Kk.original.fullsize.png\"><br />Moment of inertia about $\\mathrm{C}$ and perpendicular to the plane is :\n$\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{I} & =\\mathrm{r}^2[2+4+6] \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{3} \\times 12 \\\\\n\\mathrm{I} & =4 \\mathrm{~kg}-\\mathrm{m}^2\n\\end{aligned}$",
